course: dictionary
lesson: 12694
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them, the context, tell you which meaning is meant. The word divider comes from divide, which means to split into parts, so a divider is something that does the splitting. «We put a room divider across the hall so the twins each had a corner.»
explain: In a folder, «Put your maths work behind the blue divider.» Here a divider is a card that marks where one section ends and the next begins. The word folder is a clue that tells you which meaning fits.
explain: In maths, «Use the dividers to measure the distance between the two towns on the map.» These dividers look like a pair of compasses with two sharp points. The clues are maths and map, so this is a measuring tool. Always check: swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A divider is something that separates a space or things into parts.
fact: «Divide» means to split into parts, and a divider is the thing that does the splitting.
fact: A file divider is a card or tab that marks where one section of a folder ends.
fact: Dividers in maths are a tool with two sharp points, used to measure distances on maps.
fact: Context clues, like the words folder or map, tell you which meaning of a word is meant.
exercise: What does a divider do? | It colours the page | It joins two things into one whole | It makes things bigger | *It separates a space or things into parts
exercise: «The blue divider in my folder marks where maths begins.» What is a file divider? | A folder for storing photos | A ruler for drawing straight lines | *A card that separates sections in a folder | A small pencil case
exercise: Dad says, «Use the dividers to measure the map.» What are dividers used for in maths? | Writing names on paper | Drawing circles with paint | *Measuring distances, like compasses with two points | Cutting paper into shapes
test: «She put a room divider between the bed and the desk.» What does divider mean here? | A person who shares sweets | *Something that separates a space into parts | A type of desk lamp | A kind of bed
test: Which clue tells you that «dividers» in a sentence is a maths tool? | The word folder | The word blue | *The words map and distance | The word room
exam: Sam says a divider is always a shelf. Is he right? | *No, a divider can be a card, a room screen or a maths tool | Yes, but only in a school | No, a divider is always a person | Yes, a divider is always a shelf
